# Practical 7: Apply CI/CD Principles to Web Development Using Jenkins, Git, and a Local HTTP Server

## 1. Aim

To implement a simple **CI/CD pipeline** for a web application using **Git/GitHub, Jenkins, and a local HTTP server**, where changes pushed to GitHub are automatically deployed to the local web server.

---

## 2. What you will build

The flow will be:

```text
Developer
    │
    │ git push
    ▼
GitHub Repository
    │
    │ Jenkins detects change
    ▼
Jenkins Pipeline
    │
    ├── Checkout
    ├── Build/Validate
    └── Deploy
          │
          ▼
Local HTTP Server
          │
          ▼
http://localhost/ci-cd-demo/
```

### CI means
**Continuous Integration** — whenever code is pushed, Jenkins checks and validates the project.

### CD means
**Continuous Delivery/Deployment** — after a successful pipeline, Jenkins deploys the website automatically.

