# 11. Create the Jenkinsfile

Now create:

```text
ci-cd-web/Jenkinsfile
```

Use this Windows version:

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                echo 'Checking out source code from GitHub...'
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo 'Validating web application...'
                bat 'if not exist web\\index.html exit /b 1'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                echo 'Deploying website to local HTTP server...'

                powershell '''
                    $src = "$env:WORKSPACE\\web\\*"
                    $dest = "C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\ci-cd-demo"

                    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $dest | Out-Null

                    Copy-Item -Path $src -Destination $dest -Recurse -Force
                '''
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        success {
            echo 'CI/CD pipeline completed successfully!'
        }

        failure {
            echo 'CI/CD pipeline failed!'
        }
    }
}
```

### What this Jenkinsfile does

**Checkout:**

```groovy
checkout scm
```

Downloads the project from GitHub.

**Build:**

```groovy
if not exist web\\index.html exit /b 1
```

Checks whether the main webpage exists.

**Deploy:**

```powershell
Copy-Item
```

Copies the website into:

```text
C:\xampp\htdocs\ci-cd-demo
```

Apache then serves those files.

