## 23. Viva Questions

**Q1. What is CI?**  
Continuous Integration is the practice of automatically integrating and validating code changes frequently.

**Q2. What is CD?**  
Continuous Delivery/Deployment automates the process of delivering or deploying successfully validated code.

**Q3. What is Jenkins?**  
Jenkins is an automation server used to implement CI/CD pipelines.

**Q4. What is Git used for?**  
Git is used for version control and tracking changes to source code.

**Q5. What is GitHub?**  
GitHub is a cloud-based platform for hosting Git repositories and collaborating on source code.

**Q6. What is Apache?**  
Apache HTTP Server is a web server that serves web files to browsers.

**Q7. What is the purpose of the Jenkinsfile?**  
It defines the stages and steps of the Jenkins pipeline as code.

**Q8. What happens after `git push`?**  
In an automated setup, Jenkins can detect the change, run the pipeline, and deploy the updated website.

**Q9. What is the local HTTP server in this practical?**  
We use **Apache through XAMPP**.

**Q10. Where is the website deployed?**

```text
C:\xampp\htdocs\ci-cd-demo
```

and accessed through:

```text
http://localhost/ci-cd-demo/
```

### One-line concept to remember

> **Git stores the code → GitHub hosts it → Jenkins automates CI/CD → Apache serves the deployed website.**
